# bat configuration - %APPDATA%\bat\config on Windows; install.ps1 puts it there.
# The profile's `cat` runs `bat --paging=never`; --paging here makes plain `bat`
# behave the same way.
--paging=never
--style=numbers,changes,header

# NB: pinned, NOT --theme=auto. `auto` asks the terminal for its background over
# OSC 11, and when that query cannot be answered - a pipe, a non-TTY - bat
# silently falls back to its built-in Monokai Extended and ignores
# --theme-light/--theme-dark entirely (verified on the Linux machine). Windows
# Terminal is pinned to the Catppuccin Latte scheme, so the background is a known
# light colour and there is nothing to switch between.
#
# bat has bundled Catppuccin since 0.24: no .tmTheme to ship, no cache rebuild.
--theme="Catppuccin Latte"
